=== SURVEY ===
Surveyed all test files in internal/automation/trigger/ and internal/api/:

Broken files (stale TriggerType/TriggerConfig fields on models.Automation):
  1. internal/automation/trigger/calendar_test.go — makeCalendarAutomation returns *models.Automation
  2. internal/automation/trigger/cron_test.go — mockRepo.GetByTriggerType wrong return type,
     makeAutomation/makeOneTimeAutomation set removed fields, fire() called with wrong arity
  3. internal/api/webhook_receiver_handler_test.go — makeTestAutomation sets removed fields

Additional broken files in same package (Go compiles entire package atomically):
  4. internal/automation/trigger/webhook_test.go — same stale fields
  5. internal/automation/trigger/vehicle_state_test.go — same stale fields + wrong mock interface
  6. internal/automation/trigger/mqtt_test.go — same stale fields + wrong mock return type
  7. internal/automation/trigger/sunrise_sunset_test.go — same stale fields
  8. internal/automation/trigger/energy_test.go — stale fields + wrong repo interface (EnergyRepo)
     + shouldFireEnergy() signature changed from *EnergyConfig to *AutomationStepTriggerSignal
  9. internal/automation/trigger/geofence_test.go — stale fields + wrong repo interface (GeofenceRepo)
     + models.Geofence renamed to models.Place + snapshot field renames

=== REASONING ===
Go packages compile atomically — all test files in a package must compile for
any test or vet to succeed. The task scope listed 3 files, but 9 were broken
with the same root cause. Fixing only 3 would leave go vet failing.

Key decisions:
- mockRepo (shared across calendar/cron/sunrise_sunset/energy tests): Added
  cronAutomations ([]CronAutomation), energyAutos (map[int64][]EnergyAutomation),
  and LoadEnabledScheduleTriggers/LoadEnabledEnergySignalTriggers methods.
- makeAutomation → returns CronAutomation (was *models.Automation with stale fields)
- makeCalendarAutomation → returns *models.AutomationFull with Triggers: []any{cfg}
- makeWebhookAutomation → returns *models.AutomationFull with Triggers: []any{cfg}
- Removed 10 obsolete tests:
  - TestIsOneTimeDatePast_* (4 tests) — isOneTimeDatePast function removed
  - TestRegister_OneTime_* (3 tests) — one-time scheduling moved out of CronTrigger
  - TestFire_OneTime_* (2 tests) — fire() no longer has oneTime parameter
  - TestRegister_EmptyTriggerConfig / TestRegister_MalformedJSON — duplicates of
    existing tests; CronAutomation is typed, no JSON parsing
- Renamed TestStart_SkipsInvalid_DisablesInDB → TestStart_SkipsInvalid (ADR-012
  retired auto_disabled for schedule triggers)
- TestFire_Recurring_DoesNotDisable → TestFire_DoesNotDisable (one-time concept removed)
- energy_test.go: Added energyConfigToTrigger() bridge function mapping old EnergyConfig
  event names to AutomationStepTriggerSignal fields
- geofence_test.go: Changed mockGeofenceRepo from GetEnabledByVehicleAndTrigger to
  LoadEnabledGeofenceTriggers, changed mock data provider from *models.Geofence to *models.Place
- webhook_test.go (trigger pkg): Removed duplicate test after AutoDisabled→Disabled rename

